questions.question:
A + B means ‘A is the wife of B’;

A - B means ‘B is the daughter of A’;

A × B means ‘B is the brother of A’;

A ÷ B means ‘A is the father of B’;

If, P + R × T - Q + S ÷ U, then how is P related to the mother of U?

questions.solution:
[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2e1a2f0dc142ecfb544963c2209981c3e759d0cf81e91577dd86d50c0a2dc835.png] 

The pattern followed here is,

A + 4 = E;

E + 5 = J;

J + 6 = **P**;

P + 7 = W

Hence, “P” is the correct answer.
